    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6e1098eb-1214-5604-9a77-2e66a4708539",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following are square matrices?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $D$ is a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. It has $5$ rows and $5$ columns, so it is a $5\\times 5$ matrix.\n\n- $Q$ is a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. It has $1$ row and $1$ column, so it is a $1\\times 1$ matrix.\n\n- $S$ is a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. It has $3$ rows and $3$ columns, so it is a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\nTherefore, $D$, $Q$, and $S$ are square matrices.",
