      ":question/id": "e411a67a-8903-5923-9f4d-db9269960120",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following are square matrices?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $E$ is *not* a square matrix since the numbers of rows and columns are not the same. It has $5$ rows and $3$ columns, so it's a $5\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n- $T$ is *not* a square matrix since the numbers of rows and columns are not the same. It has $2$ rows and $5$ columns, so it's a $2\\times 5$ matrix.\n\n- $U$ is a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. It has $5$ rows and $5$ columns, so it is a $5\\times 5$ matrix.\n\nTherefore, only $U$ is a square matrix.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
